WEBVTT

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:24.900
<v Ira Glass>In Danielle's house, ever since she was a girl, when holiday dinners come, they serve a meal that will probably look familiar to you. Picture main course, big platter, drum sticks, white breast meat, golden brown skin, stuffing, and gravy, and cranberry relish on the side. And in Danielle's family they have a name for this meal that she told me on the phone recently. The name for this meal is--
<v Ira Glass>在丹妮尔家里，从小时候起，每当节日晚餐时，他们都会上一道你可能很熟悉的菜。想象一下主菜：一大盘，鸡腿、白嫩的鸡胸肉、金黄的酥皮、填料、肉汁，旁边还有蔓越莓酱。在丹妮尔的家族里，他们给这道菜起了一个名字，她最近在电话里告诉了我。这个名字是——

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.250
<v Danielle>Fish.
<v Danielle>鱼。

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.120
<v Ira Glass>Got that?
<v Ira Glass>明白了吗？

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.620
<v Danielle>Fish.
<v Danielle>鱼。

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:47.080
<v Ira Glass>Well, from WBEZ Chicago and Public Radio International, it's This American Life. A special program today on the wonders of fish.
<v Ira Glass>各位好，来自芝加哥WBEZ电台和国际公共广播电台，这里是《这个美国生活》。今天是一个关于鱼之奇迹的特别节目。

00:00:47.080 --> 00:01:40.420
<v Ira Glass>Actually, we can say the word here, and the word is poultry. And as you know, each week on our program we choose some theme, invite a variety of writers and performers to tackle that theme. And this week, as we stand now in that magical five weeks of the year, that magical five weeks between the turkey served at Thanksgiving and the turkey served at Christmas, a period when Americans consume nearly a fourth of all the turkey consumed in this country every year. And every year during this important time, This American Life brings you yet another program about poultry. That's right-- stories about turkeys, chickens, ducks, fowl of all kind, and their mysterious hold over us.
<v Ira Glass>事实上，我们可以在这里说出那个词，那个词是家禽。如你所知，我们节目的每周都会选择一个主题，邀请不同的作家和表演者来探讨这个主题。而本周，当我们正处于一年中那神奇的五周时——感恩节烤火鸡到圣诞节烤火鸡之间那神奇的五周，这期间美国人消费了全国每年近四分之一的火鸡。每年在这个重要时刻，《这个美国生活》都会为您带来一期关于家禽的节目。没错，就是关于火鸡、鸡、鸭、各种禽类以及它们对我们产生的神秘吸引力的故事。

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:57.760
<v Ira Glass>I'm Ira Glass. Coming up this hour, Act One: Duki. The story of a typical American family and imaginary poultry. Act Two: what poultry-positive program would be complete without--
<v Ira Glass>我是艾拉·格拉斯。本小时即将播出，第一幕：杜基。一个典型美国家庭与虚构家禽的故事。第二幕：如果没有这个，什么样的家禽主题节目才算完整呢——

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.240
<v Chickenman Show Chorus Member>Chickenman!
<v Chickenman Show Chorus Member>鸡侠！

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:02.200
<v Chickenman Show Chorus>He's everywhere, he's everywhere!
<v Chickenman Show Chorus>他无处不在，他无处不在！

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:41.000
<v Ira Glass>Yes, indeed. In the late 1960s, the winged warrior struck terror in the hearts of evildoers on radios all across this great nation. Today, my friends, he flies again. Act Three: Chicken Diva. In that act, an opera about Chicken Little sung in Italian, and-- no kidding-- able to make a grown man cry. Act Four: Trying To Respect The Chicken. The story of one woman's quest to try to give chickens the honor and the dignity that they are rarely accorded, even though the chickens resist her efforts.
<v Ira Glass>没错，确实如此。在20世纪60年代末，这位长翅膀的勇士在全国各地的广播电台里令恶徒们闻风丧胆。今天，我的朋友们，他再次起飞。第三幕：鸡影后。在那一幕中，有一部用意大利语演唱的关于“鸡丁”的歌剧，而且——说真的——它能让一个大男人流泪。第四幕：试图尊重鸡。故事讲述了一位女性试图赋予鸡它们很少享有的荣誉和尊严，尽管鸡群抵制她的努力。

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:52.250
<v Ira Glass>Stay with us.
<v Ira Glass>请继续收听。

00:02:52.250 --> 00:03:01.950
<v Ira Glass>Act One: Duki. So in Danielle's family, the power of poultry is so great in their lives that when they serve chicken or turkey, they call it--
<v Ira Glass>第一幕：杜基。在丹妮尔的家族里，家禽在他们的生活中有着巨大的影响力，以至于当他们上鸡肉或火鸡时，他们称之为——

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:02.540
<v Danielle>Fish.
<v Danielle>鱼。

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:10.130
<v Ira Glass>That's right. And they call it this for a reason. And the reason has to do with a stuffed hand puppet called Duki.
<v Ira Glass>没错。他们这样称呼是有原因的。这个原因与一个名叫杜基的毛绒手偶有关。

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:17.600
<v Ira Glass>Now, Danielle, is a woman over 30 years old. Her sister Ashley is two years younger. Duki has been in the family since they were children.
<v Ira Glass>丹妮尔今年30多岁了。她的妹妹阿什利比她小两岁。杜基在他们还是孩子的时候就已经在家里了。

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:58.050
<v Danielle>Well, he was a Christmas present when Ashley was about 8 and I was about 10. And when he first arrived, he was really fluffy. And he was this beautiful, fluffy, white duck. He had a cape on and black kind of villain slash hero goggles. He lost the outfit pretty quickly and he went naked. And then he became Ashley's vehicle for torturing me.
<v Danielle>嗯，它是阿什利大约8岁、我10岁那年的圣诞礼物。刚到家时，它非常蓬松。那是一只漂亮、毛茸茸的白鸭子。它披着斗篷，戴着黑色的反派兼英雄护目镜。它很快就弄丢了那身行头，光秃秃的了。后来它成了阿什利折磨我的工具。

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:19.950
<v Ira Glass>It's not unusual for older siblings to dominate younger ones. And as children, Danielle dominated Ashley. Ashley looked up to Danielle, fought to get her attention and her approval, and Danielle always, always got her way. Except when Duki was around.
<v Ira Glass>年长的兄弟姐妹支配年幼的往往很常见。小时候，丹妮尔总是压制阿什利。阿什利仰慕丹妮尔，争取她的关注和认可，而丹妮尔总是随心所欲。除了杜基在场的时候。

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:42.810
<v Ira Glass>Basically, Ashley would channel-- I mean, the word's kind of an anachronism in this context-- but she would channel Duki. She would become Duki's voice. She would speak as Duki. And Duki was sarcastic. Duki was selfish and bossy. Duki would insult Danielle. Duki would tease Danielle. Duki would give her painful nose squeaks.
<v Ira Glass>基本上，阿什利会附身——我是说，在这种语境下这个词有点时代错误——但她会通过杜基说话。她会成为杜基的代言人。杜基非常刻薄。杜基自私又霸道。杜基会侮辱丹妮尔，嘲弄丹妮尔。杜基还会捏她的鼻子发出吱吱声。

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:52.860
<v Danielle>Whenever Ashley brought Duki into the equation, he was completely the dominant force. I was just putty in Duki's hands.
<v Danielle>每当阿什利把杜基带入这种状态，它就成了绝对的主导力量。我在杜基手中就像橡皮泥一样任人摆布。

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:59.060
<v Ira Glass>Let me ask you to compare his personality with Ashley's personality.
<v Ira Glass>让我请你比较一下它和阿什利的性格。

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:30.250
<v Danielle>Ashley is very kind of considerate, and-- she's very considerate and kind and thoughtful. And very, very sensitive to other people. Very, very concerned about if other people are happy and if someone or someone else doesn't feel good. And Duki has this total, like, you know, what's for lunch attitude. Like what's in it for me, in your face, totally out for himself. Simultaneously a braggart and a total wimp.
<v Danielle>阿什利非常体贴，而且——她非常有同情心、善良且细心。非常非常在意别人的感受，关心别人是否快乐，或者别人是否不舒服。而杜基完全是一种“午餐吃什么”的态度。就好像“我能从中得到什么”，很直白，完全为自己着想。既是一个吹牛大王，又是个彻头彻尾的懦夫。

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:32.230
<v Ira Glass>He's boastful and vain.
<v Ira Glass>它既自大又虚荣。

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:47.190
<v Danielle>He's just this indomitable-- yeah-- indomitable spirit.
<v Danielle>它就是那种不屈不挠的——是的——不屈不挠的精神。

00:05:47.190 --> 00:06:07.300
<v Ira Glass>All right. I've been at Daniels apartment sometimes, and I've witnessed the following scene-- picture, please. Danielle has not spoken with her sister in weeks. She picks up the phone, calls Ashley in Michigan. Ashley answers. Danielle asks immediately, "can you put Duki on?"
<v Ira Glass>好了。我有时在丹妮尔的公寓里，目睹过以下场景——请想象一下。丹妮尔已经几周没和她妹妹说话了。她拿起电话，打给密歇根州的阿什利。阿什利接了电话。丹妮尔立刻问：“能让杜基接电话吗？”

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:30.000
<v Ira Glass>And then Ashley essentially becomes Duki, puts Duki on the phone. Danielle talks to Duki for 15, 20 minutes. And then they both hang up. That's the whole conversation. And they both feel satisfied. These are adult-- Danielle is an editor at a big New York magazine.
<v Ira Glass>然后阿什利基本上就变成了杜基，让杜基接电话。丹妮尔和杜基聊了15、20分钟。然后他们都挂了电话。这就是整个对话。他们都感到满足。这些都是成年人——丹妮尔是纽约一家大型杂志社的编辑。

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:56.740
<v Danielle>I adore Duki. I really love Duki. And sometimes I think if he disappeared, it would really feel like someone died. I mean, I look at him and he looks really kind of old and ratty, and it really makes me sad. I feel like-- it sounds crazy. It really makes me sad to think about a world without Duki. And that it would be a big empty hole the world.
<v Danielle>我爱杜基。我真的很爱杜基。有时我觉得如果它消失了，真的会感觉像死了亲人一样。我是说，看着它，它看起来真的很旧、很破烂，这让我很难过。我觉得——这听起来很疯狂。一想到没有杜基的世界，我就真的很伤心。那会是世界上一个巨大的空洞。

00:06:56.740 --> 00:07:18.070
<v Danielle>He kind of takes up as much room in my heart as a lot of people individually. And if something happened to him, you know, if he were lost at an airport or run over by a car, it would really be heartbreaking.
<v Danielle>它在我心中的位置，和许多人作为个体在我心中的位置一样重。如果它发生了什么意外，比如在机场丢了或者被车轧了，真的会让人心碎。

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:30.590
<v Ira Glass>So I hope it's becoming clear why, if you eat dinner in the home of Danielle's family, if they're serving some kind of poultry-- you know, chicken or turkey-- if you were to ask anybody in the family, "what's for dinner," they'll tell you--
<v Ira Glass>所以我想现在很清楚了，为什么如果你在丹妮尔家里吃晚饭，如果他们上的是禽肉——比如鸡肉或火鸡——如果你问家里任何人“晚饭吃什么”，他们会告诉你——

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:31.080
<v Danielle>Fish.
<v Danielle>鱼。

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:34.930
<v Ira Glass>Right. And the rationale for that is what?
<v Ira Glass>没错。那么理由是什么呢？

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:36.130
<v Danielle>It freaks Duki out.
<v Danielle>那会把杜基吓坏的。

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:42.740
<v Ira Glass>It freaks him out, though-- you don't like him to know that perhaps some birds are, in fact, eaten?
<v Ira Glass>这会吓坏它，不过——你不希望它知道事实上有些鸟类确实是被吃掉的？

00:07:42.740 --> 00:08:02.300
<v Danielle>I think he knows. I think he's in denial about it. He's in denial about most things. He's in denial about the fact that he's totally weak and tiny and dirty. He thinks he's really good looking and strong. And that he's really smart and has a lot of friends.
<v Danielle>我想它是知道的。我想它对此在进行自我否认。它对大多数事情都在否认。它否认自己其实很虚弱、渺小又肮脏的事实。它认为自己长得很帅、很强壮，而且它很聪明，有很多朋友。

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:24.110
<v Danielle>He's in denial about the fact that he's actually stuffed, which he is. Sometimes I tell him, and I say, "Duki, give me a break-- you're just stuffed." And he's like, "no way."
<v Danielle>它否认自己其实是个填充玩具的事实，而它确实是。有时我告诉它，我说：“杜基，饶了我吧，你只是个填充玩具。”它就说：“才不是呢。”

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:51.440
<v Ira Glass>Now, I thought I would try to book Duki to come on the radio for this program. So I contacted Danielle's sister Ashley and asked her, you know, "could Duki come on the air?" I received an answer back not by phone, but by electronic mail that for Duki to appear, I'd have to first go through someone named Yona Lu, who I could reach through Danielle and Ashley's mother. And when I talked to Danielle, I asked her about this.
<v Ira Glass>现在，我想尝试预约杜基来参加这个节目的广播。所以我联系了丹妮尔的妹妹阿什利，问她：“杜基能上节目吗？”我收到的回复不是通过电话，而是通过电子邮件。她说如果杜基要上节目，我必须先通过一个叫约娜·卢的人，我可以联系丹妮尔和阿什利的妈妈。当我和丹妮尔谈话时，我问了这件事。

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:58.580
<v Ira Glass>I've been informed that the only way that I can reach him is by calling your mom and speaking to Yona Lu? Do I have that name right?
<v Ira Glass>我被告知联系它的唯一方法是打给你妈妈，和约娜·卢交谈？那个名字我没记错吧？

00:08:58.580 --> 00:08:59.780
<v Danielle>Yona Lu, yeah.
<v Danielle>约娜·卢，是的。

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:00.240
<v Ira Glass>Yona Lu.
<v Ira Glass>约娜·卢。

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:02.510
<v Danielle>I think that's-- she's acting as his agent.
<v Danielle>我想那是——她在担任它的经纪人。

00:09:02.510 --> 00:09:03.840
<v Ira Glass>Yona Lu is?
<v Ira Glass>约娜·卢是吗？

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:07.940
<v Danielle>She's a hedgehog.
<v Danielle>她是一只刺猬。

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:13.190
<v Ira Glass>Anything special that I should say to Yona Lu to make this happen?
<v Ira Glass>有什么特别的话是我该对约娜·卢说的，好让这件事促成吗？

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:17.380
<v Danielle>I mean, I don't know. She's a pretty-- she drives a pretty hard bargain.
<v Danielle>我是说，我不知道。她挺……她很难讨价还价的。

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:18.330
<v Danielle>[PHONE RINGING]
<v Danielle>[电话铃声]

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:19.270
<v Mrs. Mattoon>Hello?
<v Mrs. Mattoon>喂？

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:20.160
<v Ira Glass>Hey, Mrs. Mattoon?
<v Ira Glass>嘿，马通太太？

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:20.610
<v Mrs. Mattoon>Yes.
<v Mrs. Mattoon>是。

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:21.930
<v Ira Glass>It's Ira Glass.
<v Ira Glass>我是艾拉·格拉斯。

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:23.420
<v Mrs. Mattoon>Hi, Ira Glass.
<v Mrs. Mattoon>你好，艾拉·格拉斯。

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:30.440
<v Ira Glass>Mrs. Mattoon, here's why I called you. I want to do a little story on the radio about Duki.
<v Ira Glass>马通太太，我打电话是这样，我想在广播里做一段关于杜基的小故事。

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:31.060
<v Mrs. Mattoon>Duki.
<v Mrs. Mattoon>杜基。

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:33.470
<v Ira Glass>Duki.
<v Ira Glass>杜基。

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:42.320
<v Ira Glass>And I contacted your daughter Ashley, and she said that for me to book Duki onto my radio show, I was going to first need to contact Yona Lu.
<v Ira Glass>我联系了你女儿阿什利，她说如果要预约杜基上我的广播节目，我需要先联系约娜·卢。

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:44.760
<v Mrs. Mattoon>Yona Lu. [LAUGHING]
<v Mrs. Mattoon>约娜·卢。[笑]

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:46.080
<v Mrs. Mattoon>Yeah, you would need to do that.
<v Mrs. Mattoon>是的，你需要这样做。

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:47.970
<v Ira Glass>And that I needed to do that through you.
<v Ira Glass>并且我需要通过你来做这件事。

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:49.220
<v Mrs. Mattoon>Yeah.
<v Mrs. Mattoon>是的。

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:50.280
<v Ira Glass>Who is Yona Lu.
<v Ira Glass>约娜·卢是谁？

00:09:50.280 --> 00:10:04.610
<v Mrs. Mattoon>Yona Lu is-- she's a hedgehog. She's basically taken charge of Duki's financial affairs. And I presume this is something to do with money?
<v Mrs. Mattoon>约娜·卢是——她是一只刺猬。她基本上接管了杜基的财务事务。我想这和钱有关？

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:07.160
<v Ira Glass>Well, I don't know, actually. I mean, we--
<v Ira Glass>嗯，事实上我也不知道。我是说，我们——

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:10.060
<v Mrs. Mattoon>That's probably why she said to contact Yona Lu.
<v Mrs. Mattoon>那可能就是她让你联系约娜·卢的原因。

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:19.550
<v Ira Glass>Well, so what do I do now? I'm calling-- I was told to contact you if I wanted to get in touch with Yona Lu in order to book Duki. What do I do next?
<v Ira Glass>嗯，那我该怎么办？我打电话——我被告知如果想联系约娜·卢来预约杜基，就要联系你。接下来我该做什么？

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.580
<v Mrs. Mattoon>Book Duki, OK. You're gonna' book Duki?
<v Mrs. Mattoon>预约杜基，好。你要预约杜基？

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:25.720
<v Ira Glass>That's the whole idea. I want to book Duki for the show for an interview.
<v Ira Glass>就是这个想法。我想预约杜基来节目接受采访。

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:32.860
<v Mrs. Mattoon>Well, I'll just talk to Yona Lu about it. She says OK, it's OK.
<v Mrs. Mattoon>嗯，我会和约娜·卢谈谈。她说可以，那就没问题。

